            "heading": "Ordered By How Far They Can Scale",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "We ranked the ideas by how far income and independence can stretch with skill and proof, not by how fashionable they look."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Tutoring, notes, campus services and home-made products come next, because they need a business layer such as a course, a bundle or a brand."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "ideas",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 2
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:4",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Fitting a Business Around Studies",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Study comes first because the exam is the entry requirement to your next stage."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "A college seat should take only a small share of that budget (we use about 10 percent as a starting guide), and the rest has to stay free for living, tools and learning."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Treat it as a practice project."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "study-balance",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 4
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:7",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Commit to One Idea, Put",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Do you like talking to customers, or do you prefer working alone with headphones."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Pick the idea your energy can survive in exam month."
              }
            ],
